- **Mutation, query and CSSOM:** `doc.mutate()` methods `create_element`, `create_text_node`, `set_attribute`, `clear_attribute`, `append_children`, `insert_nodes_before`, `remove_node`, `remove_and_drop_node`, `set_inner_html`, `set_node_text`, `set_custom_widget`, `set_style_property` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/detached_attribute.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/incremental_oracle.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/incremental_oracle.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/incremental_oracle.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/incremental_oracle.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/custom_widget_layout.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/line_break.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/animations.rs:); selector API `query_selector`, `query_selector_all`, `query_selector_in`, `query_selector_all_in`, `matches_selector`, `closest`, `try_parse_selector_list` and node-level raw variants, returning `Result` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/scoped_query_selector.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/scoped_query_selector.rs:), as `Result<Option<NodeId>, ParseError>` / `Result<SmallVec<[NodeId; 32]>, ParseError>` never matching the scope node (packages/blitz-dom/src/query_selector.rs:; packages/blitz-dom/src/query_selector.rs:); CSSOM addresses stylesheets by owner `NodeId` and rules by an index path (packages/blitz-dom/src/cssom.rs:) with `CssRuleInfo` snapshots (packages/blitz-dom/src/cssom.rs:); `resolved_style_value` returns an empty string for unknown properties and used values for layout-dependent ones (packages/blitz-dom/src/resolved_style.rs:); `RequestContentType` urlencoded, multipart, text/plain (packages/blitz-dom/src/form.rs:); `BoundingRect { x, y, width, height }` in f64 (packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:); `build_accessibility_tree` returns an accesskit `TreeUpdate` of `(NodeId, accesskit::Node)` pairs, naming a node from five sources
 — its direct text children (`labelled_by` its `TextRun`s), an `aria-label` non-empty after trimming (`label`, accname-1.2 §2C), a `<label>` bound through `label_bound_input_element` (its `for`-target labelable element by id, else its first nested labelable element — HTML's labelable elements, `button`, an `input` whose `type` is not `hidden` (ASCII case-insensitive), `meter`, `output`, `progress`, `select` and `textarea`, matched by the private `is_labelable`), pushed onto the bound element's `labelled_by` after the visit when both have built nodes, a select's option's non-empty `label` attribute where it has no `aria-label`, and an `optgroup`'s (`Role::Group`), named in the tree and painted as a header in an open list (packages/blitz-dom/src/accessibility.rs:; packages/blitz-dom/src/accessibility.rs:; packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:; packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:), and, since the 2026-10-17 upstream sync (upstream's reads as upstream wrote them, merged at `23b9b26a9`), `aria-labelledby`: after the `<label>` → input loop it clears the node's `labelled_by`, pushes the referenced nodes that have built nodes (an id naming no element ignored, `referenced_dom_ids_to_node_ids`) and sets their text, gathered through `write_text_alternative` · `write_flat_text_content` · `FlatText`, as the computed `label` (`set_label`), so it outranks a `<label>` and an `aria-label` (accname 2B over 2C/2D), the `aria-label` the fallback when the targets hold no text (packages/blitz-dom/src/accessibility.rs:; packages/blitz-dom/src/accessibility.rs:; packages/blitz-dom/src/accessibility.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/accessibility_label.rs:);
 the same sync's builder also reads `aria-describedby` (the referenced built nodes pushed as `described_by`), `aria-description` (its own text into AccessKit's description field), `aria-expanded` (a boolean, a single select excepted, which reads none and writes `expanded` from its list), `aria-disabled` (`true` sets AccessKit disabled) and `aria-level` (a number, with defaults by tag and role, `default_level_for_tag` · `default_level_for_role`), then `set_html_tag` last (packages/blitz-dom/src/accessibility.rs:; packages/blitz-dom/src/accessibility.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/accessibility_description.rs:); our trimmed non-empty `aria-label` read and the closed-set `aria-selected` · `aria-pressed` · `aria-invalid` reads below are kept, and upstream's own `aria-selected` (`parse::<bool>`) and unfiltered `aria-label` reads were dropped in the merge, so the builder reads each attribute once; since 2026-10-10-snapshot-states the builder (`BaseDocument::build_accessibility_node`, private) also reads state attributes on every element — a select's option excepted, whose `selected` is its chosen state, true or false, with no `aria-selected` read (packages/blitz-dom/src/accessibility.rs:) —, the toggle by role, each value trimmed of ASCII whitespace and compared exactly, in lower case — `aria-selected`: `true` / `false` sets AccessKit `selected` true / false, anything else nothing; `aria-pressed`: `true` · `false` · `mixed` sets `toggled` `True` · `False` · `Mixed`, anything else nothing, on every role but the five checkable ones; `aria-checked`: the same three values set `toggled` on a role in the private `is_checkable` set — `CheckBox` · `Switch` · `RadioButton` · `MenuItemCheckBox` · `MenuItemRadio` — and on no other, `role_from_name` mapping `"switch"` to `Role::Switch`;
 a native `input` whose `type` is exactly `checkbox` or `radio` (the private `is_native_checkable`) reads neither, its native checkedness winning (HTML-AAM), and the builder writes `toggled` from that native checked state under a checkable role (below), so the tree states it as the snapshot's `checked` reads the element — the toggle read per role ratified by the founder (2026-10-18); `aria-invalid`: `true` · `grammar` · `spelling` sets `invalid` `True` · `Grammar` · `Spelling`, an absent, empty (after trimming) or `false` value nothing, and any other value `Invalid::True` (WAI-ARIA 1.2's rule for a value outside the allowed list); the lower-case exact match is a choice — the specification as read states no case rule and no browser was measured — so `TRUE` reads unrecognized: nothing for `aria-selected`, `aria-pressed` and `aria-checked`, invalid for `aria-invalid`; each attribute is read once, and only these reads and that native write set `toggled`; the added lines hold no log site and no panic path — a value of 5,500 characters builds the tree — so what `build_accessibility_tree` returns changes for every document whose markup states one of the four (packages/blitz-dom/src/accessibility.rs:; packages/blitz-dom/src/accessibility.rs:; packages/blitz-dom/src/accessibility.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/accessibility_states.rs: — as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-10-snapshot-states/report.md); blitz-shell builds the platform tree through the document trait
 — `AccessibilityState::update_tree(&dyn Document)` calls `doc.accessibility_tree()`, from `View::poll` and from `View::build_accessibility_tree` on `InitialTreeRequested`: on a poll that reported work `View::poll` takes the document's changed set (`take_changed_nodes`, outside the `accessibility` cfg, so a shell built without the feature still drains the set and drops it) and, under `accessibility`, calls `update_tree` when the set it took was non-empty — so the platform accessibility adapter receives the tree on change as well as on its initial request, the same crossing and the same content classes (ids as `author_id`, accessible names), more often; since 2026-10-10-snapshot-states the nodes it is handed carry a third content class, states — `selected`, `toggled` and `invalid` on each element node whose markup states them, a native control's `toggled` and a `multiple` select's multiselectable beside them, closed enums and booleans, never an attribute's value as typed — a widening of the adapter crossing ratified by the founder (2026-10-10, by question dialog in the overseer session, relayed verbatim by the overseer as his chosen option label «Ратифицировать», the English wording is the overseer's: the builder writes the three states on the node), what an assistive technology reads of them unmeasured until a windowed check — no stand binary builds a platform adapter and the dev host's AT-SPI bus reads inactive — and that witness owned by residual `res-llkgqygv`, re-carried at 0.3.0 (target: next), at an active assistive technology this version does not reach, on the founder's F1 «Пока нет, перенести (Рекомендую)» (2026-10-14), whose headless halves — the tree the shell hands the adapter, read through `&dyn Document`, and the refresh on a Tab and an Enter — are proven on the stand since 2026-10-14-stand-a11y-assertions (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_accessibility_ids.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_accessibility_ids.rs:);
 since the 2026-10-17 upstream sync the names class also carries `aria-labelledby`'s computed text, and the nodes carry a fourth content class, descriptions — `aria-description`'s own page text (free, unbounded) and `aria-describedby`'s targets as `described_by` — to the adapter only (the snapshot reads no description), a widening by upstream merge ratified as upstream's behaviour by the founder (2026-10-17, by question dialog in the overseer session, relayed by the overseer, «Утвердить оба (Рекомендую)», both sources confirmed by his «Подтвердить все 10 (Рекомендую)», 2026-10-18), and `aria-expanded` · `aria-disabled` · `aria-level` closed values inside the states class, and a single select's `expanded` a closed bool from engine state, unmeasured at an assistive technology like the states; what the poll reads, and before 2026-10-07-change-tracking-and-diff the poll-time refresh did not run (§Document core), so the platform tree was built once; ratified by the founder (2026-10-07) — the shell half of one item with the engine's changed-set contract, "refresh, then drain"; its windowed witness is still owed: no windowed run witnesses the refresh on the dev host — its AT-SPI bus reads inactive and the stand's windowed binary builds blitz-shell without `accessibility` — so it is held by the document-level tests and both feature builds of blitz-shell (packages/blitz-shell/src/accessibility.rs:; packages/blitz-shell/src/window.rs:; packages/blitz-shell/src/window.rs:) — as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-change-tracking-and-diff/report.md (packages/blitz-dom/src/accessibility.rs:; packages/blitz-dom/src/accessibility.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/accessibility_roles.rs:); `HtmlDocument` API `from_html`, `query_selector`, `mutate().set_inner_html`, `resolve`, `root_element().final_layout()` (examples/inner_html.rs:; examples/screenshot.rs:)

- **tests/blitz-tests:** holds Blitz's integration tests, one test-target file per behavior under `tests/`, and three shared modules that are no target — `tests/common/mod.rs`, the stand checks' tables and helpers, each stated once, `tests/session_common/mod.rs`, what the checks that hold a session share, and, since 2026-10-19-shared-fixtures, `tests/fixtures/mod.rs`, the fixture boot and hold, the fixture pages more than one check reads and the held network stand-in `HeldNet`, each stated once (§3 Crate-local test helpers) (tests/blitz-tests/lib.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/Cargo.toml:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/common/mod.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/session_common/mod.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/fixtures/mod.rs:), and one file that is declared a target and never built, `tests/all.rs` — upstream's single-binary target `all`, held in the manifest at `test = false` (§2 Directory pattern; tests/blitz-tests/Cargo.toml:); coverage spans accessibility, layout, text, paint, hit testing, input events, scrolling, style invalidation, DOM mutation leaks, network-driven stylesheet loading, four checks that arrived with the 2026-10-10 upstream merge — autofocus read by the attribute's presence (`autofocus_attribute`, 5), the `math-auto` text transform (`text_transform`, 3), an anonymous block keeping its percentage-height containing block (`anonymous_block_percentage_height`, 1) and an inline box's offset size under three writing modes (one test of `inline_fragment_rects`), the package's blitz-dom dev-dependency gaining the `autofocus` and `text-transform-icu` features for them (tests/blitz-tests/tests/autofocus_attribute.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/text_transform.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/anonymous_block_percentage_height.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/inline_fragment_rects.rs:;
 tests/blitz-tests/Cargo.toml:) —, five that arrived with the 2026-10-13 upstream merge (`434e0661`), each its own target — a restyled owner's anonymous-block text following it (`anonymous_block_restyle`, 10), a button and a button-like input centring their content after `default.css`'s button-input rule became `inline-block` (`button_alignment`, 16), removing `checked` unchecking a checkbox and a radio (`checked_attribute`, 2), a pointer leaving the document, a sub-document host or the window, or a finger lifted or cancelled, clearing hover with leave events (`pointer_leave`, 7, through a hand-written `ShellProvider`), and `DocumentConfig.ua_stylesheets` used as given, the default config taking the default sheet and a later sheet overriding an earlier (`ua_stylesheet_order`, 3) — the package gaining the dev-dependency `cursor-icon` for them (tests/blitz-tests/tests/anonymous_block_restyle.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/button_alignment.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/checked_attribute.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/pointer_leave.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/ua_stylesheet_order.rs:) —, Dioxus integration (including the clearing of a falsy Dioxus `disabled`, tests/blitz-tests/tests/dioxus_falsy_disabled.rs:, and of each of the 28 boolean attributes the check names — the bridge's own list until 2026-10-13-upstream-sync-polish-and-ship, its predicate since then upstream's 28-name `is_bool_attr` (`inert` added), and since 2026-10-13-stand-keyboard-harness `inert` the check's 28th name (`BOOLEAN_ATTRS: [&str; 28]`), the attribute half only, `stand_keyboard` and `inert_subtree` pinning a truthy `inert` honoured, a falsy one cleared by the bridge — on both attribute paths and in both layout modes — a `hidden: false` element displayed and a snapshot node, a truthy or unlisted attribute kept
 — tests/blitz-tests/tests/dioxus_falsy_boolean_attrs.rs:), the seven_guis headless stand — each lean task mounted in TaskShell offline at the pinned viewport with the bundled font, fresh-boot and incremental `dom_string` identity, one driven interaction per task, timer ticks, one stable element id per element in both layout modes, the same id across a re-render, a remount (fresh `NodeId`s bar the four document-skeleton elements) and a fresh process — the test binary re-executing its own `#[ignore]` child `ids_in_a_child_process` — and the id carried as AccessKit `author_id` on every element node and none other, the 14 controls' roles and names — and since 2026-10-14-stand-a11y-assertions every tree node of the four lean tasks in the nine interactive roles named, at least `controls(task).len()` of them per task, `crud-list` reading `People` in the tree and the snapshot by `common::REGION_NAMES`; the tree read through `&dyn blitz_dom::Document`, the call `AccessibilityState::update_tree` makes, equal to `harness.doc.accessibility_tree()` and carrying on every `author_id` its node's `element_id`, none empty, all digits or holding `0x`; and after a drained changed set a Tab and an Enter each leaving `has_changes()` true, that tree's focus and `counter-value`'s name following (`stand_accessibility_ids` 8, 5 until then, run by the `a11y` leg since then; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_accessibility_ids.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_accessibility_ids.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_accessibility_ids.rs:) —, the ids after a re-render and the Tab order of `common::tab_order` — CRUD's restated at 2026-10-13-stand-keyboard-harness to six stops, `back-btn`, `crud-filter`, `crud-list`, `crud-name`, `crud-surname`, `crud-create` (five until then), the three other tasks' unchanged, and each lean task's snapshot in both layout modes
 — every node carrying id, role, name, state and bounds, its ids the accessibility tree's `author_id`s, its roles and names that tree's, the tree following the TaskShell, each control rendered at boot inside the viewport at its bounding client rect, state as the engine reads it, the snapshot deterministic and following a re-render, each control's state proven through real input in both layout modes — a disabled control reading not enabled until the app enables it (a `disabled="false"` and a bare `disabled` in parsed markup included), typed text reading back as the value, the range input reading the app's duration, exactly the focused control reading focused after a click, a Tab press and Shift+Tab, since 2026-10-10-snapshot-states exactly the chosen flight type's option reading selected and the reading swapping with the choice, exactly the selected CRUD row reading selected across a move, a Delete and a filter edit, and a date that is no date reading invalid on both date inputs — no other node reading pressed, selected or invalid, and every node's three readings asserted equal to its accessibility node's by the file's `stated` helper (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_snapshot_state.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_snapshot_state.rs:) —, and, on an in-file fixture booted with the stand's options, a checkbox and a radio reading checked after a click, a typed password reading the fixed mask and appearing in no snapshot or accessibility-tree field, and a textarea named by `aria-label` reading empty before typing and its typed text back as its value, exactly it reading focused after the click (`a_textarea_reads_back_typed_text`, the eighth test the file gained, of eleven since 2026-10-10-snapshot-states, read red with the `textarea` arm of the snapshot's `value` deleted — the one mutant the Epoch 4 code audit left alive
 — and green on the restored tree: tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_snapshot_state.rs:, as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-09-audit-corrections-agent-surfaces/evidence/controls.md) —, each lean task's screen as the snapshot's text (`Snapshot::to_text`) in both layout modes — one line per snapshot node carrying its role, name, id, state and bounds, nested by indent, every id on exactly one line, each screen under its in-file ceiling and under `SNAPSHOT_TEXT_BUDGET` (10,000 bytes; the largest, Crud, reads 2049 since 2026-10-10-snapshot-states — 2034 before it), CRUD after one Create longer and still inside it, the text the same across two calls, the two layout modes and a second boot, `focused` on no line at boot and on exactly `back-btn`'s after a Tab press, and, on two fixtures booted with the stand's options — the shared password page `fixtures::password_labelled` and an in-file file-input page —, a typed password and a file input's authored path reading the quoted mask and occurring nowhere in the text —, the diff of the snapshots taken before and after a step (`Snapshot::diff`) in both layout modes — a click on `counter-increment` naming `counter-value`, Create naming the new row added and Delete naming it removed, a click on a text input, a Tab press and Shift+Tab each naming exactly the controls whose `focused` reading moved, a typed character naming its text input, delivered ticks naming the elapsed time and the progress bar they widen, a pump with nothing pending on each lean task and a click on a disabled control reading an empty diff and a false `has_changes`, every step held against the file's own reading of the two snapshots and equal across the two layout modes, and, on three fixtures booted with the stand's options
 — two in-file and the shared password page `fixtures::password_labelled` —, an element hidden and shown by attribute leaving and returning with its descendants, a typed password named once and only by the fixed mask, and a rewritten label naming the input it labels —, the ids held across code edits — a before/after pair of same-named components per edit, in both layout modes: each lean task under an edited shell, keyed elements under every edit, anchored elements under an edit outside their anchor, a behaviour edit, and the edits inside an anchor measured on positional ids only — and every actionable element of the four lean tasks and of Home reading an author key (`DioxusDocument::unkeyed_actionable` empty) in both layout modes and across state, and, since 2026-10-14-stand-requirement-sweep, of all seven tasks — `unkeyed_actionable()` 0 · 0 · 0 on Temperature Converter · Circle Drawer · Cells in both layout modes (2 · 3 · 676 until then), Circle Drawer's dialog open included, the three tasks keyed by added `id:` lines alone (`temp-celsius`, `temp-fahrenheit`, `circle-undo`, `circle-redo`, `circle-canvas`, `circle-diameter`, `circle-close`, `cell-{A..Z}{0..25}` on the 676 data cells, `cell-input`, and `cells-grid`, the grid's own id, taken with `tabindex` 0, `aria_label` `Cells` and an `onkeydown`, with no role), no CSS selecting by them and no other markup line moved (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_actionable_keys.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_actionable_keys.rs:) (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_id_edits.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_actionable_keys.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_snapshot.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_accessibility_ids.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_boot.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_counter.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_flight_booker.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_timer.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_crud.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_element_ids.rs:;
 tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_id_persistence.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_snapshot_state.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_snapshot_text.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_diff.rs:) — accessible names from `aria-label` and `<label>` association, and a plain document's tree carrying no `author_id` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/accessibility_names.rs:) — and, since 2026-10-10-snapshot-states, the accessibility builder's three state attributes read by value on a parsed page, in both layout modes — `accessibility_states` 6: `aria-selected` reads `true` and `false` and nothing else (9 rows), `aria-pressed` its three values and nothing else (10), `aria-invalid` its values and an unrecognized one as true (11), each on a role that supports the attribute and one that does not, the row counts asserted; `aria-checked`'s `true` · `false` · `mixed` written as the toggle on the five checkable roles alone, and a native checkbox or radio reading neither author attribute and writing `toggled` from its checked state (`aria_checked_reads_its_three_values_on_a_checkable_role_alone`); and `aria-pressed` on a checkable role reading nothing, a 5,500-character `aria-checked` nowhere in the tree (`aria_pressed_on_a_checkable_role_reads_nothing_and_a_long_aria_checked_is_nowhere`) (tests/blitz-tests/tests/accessibility_states.rs:), run by the workspace `test` leg, per package, the `stand-repeat` leg (a named `--test` of its list) and the `a11y` leg, one of its fourteen files; blitz-dom holds no unit test of the builder's reads, and no check reads the three states as the platform adapter hands them to an assistive technology — no stand binary builds an adapter and the dev host's AT-SPI bus reads inactive, the stand's normal dependency graph holding neither `accesskit_xplat` nor `accesskit_winit` (`cargo tree --locked -p seven_guis -e normal` probe 0, as measured at escher-0.2.0/chunks/2026-10-24-a11y-re-read/report.md), so no check in the `a11y` leg reaches the adapter crossing
